    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0047" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg40"/>

                <head>No. 24.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Braida to Mr. Uhl</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 11.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    decree issued last night and sent to me by the Honorable Minister Don José
                    Madriz.</p>
                <p>I beg to remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. C. Braida</hi></signed></closer>
                <pb facs="0048" n="41" xml:id="pg41"/>
                <postscript>
                    <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Postscript.]</seg></opener>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps">Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1894-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March
                                    31, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                    <p>I beg to add to my dispatch of the 29th instant a statement from the American
                        citizens in answer to a written request from Minister Don Jose Madriz
                        regarding complaints and wishes of our citizens, copy of which was forwarded
                        to said minister yesterday.</p>
                </postscript>




